# Never ship .brd files. board authors brand files itself; it never ships
# pre-made brand files (see README.md), and every existing *.brd that entered
# this repo did so by accident. A blanket deny here is the structural
# guarantee: even if one is added to the index by mistake, a fresh clone will
# never push one.
*.brd

.DS_Store

# Sample .brd files are local test fixtures, never shipped. The test suite
# (tests/run-tests.sh + tests/forge_brd.py, which deliberately writes
# malformed/hostile .brd files to prove the decoder rejects them) stays local
# too: real, useful test coverage, just not something to publish alongside the
# public repo without more thought about how a "forge" tool reads out of
# context. Keep using it locally: `make test` still works from a checkout
# that has it, it's just not tracked or shipped from here on.
/tests/

# Build output
/Build/
/build/
*.o
